      "> [!WARNING]\n> **CRITICAL DEADLINE DIFFERENTIATION:**\n> - **MS / M.Phil Programmes & Need-Based Scholarships:** Close **TODAY, 05 October 2026**.\n> - **Undergraduate BS, Associate Degrees (AD), B.Ed & Diplomas:** Close on **10 October 2026**.\n> - **Commencement of Fall 2026 Classes:** Scheduled for **12 October 2026**.",
      "### Quick Overview Summary Table",
      "- **Institution:** Virtual University of Pakistan (Federal Chartered Public University)\n- **Intake Session:** Fall 2026 Admissions\n- **MS / M.Phil Application Deadline:** 05 October 2026 (Closes Today!)\n- **Need-Based Scholarship Deadline:** 05 October 2026 (Closes Today!)\n- **General Undergraduate & Diploma Deadline:** 10 October 2026\n- **Course Exemption / Credit Transfer Deadline:** 10 October 2026\n- **Processing Fee Deposit Deadline:** 10 October 2026\n- **Change of Study Program Deadline:** 11 October 2026\n- **Commencement of Academic Classes:** 12 October 2026\n- **Course Selection (Add/Drop) Deadline:** 21 October 2026\n- **Admission Processing Fee:** Rs. 500/- (Payable online or via bank challan)\n- **Study Modes:** Campus-Based (over 200 campuses) or Home-Based (Distance e-Learning)\n- **Official Application Portal:** [www.vu.edu.pk/apply](https://www.vu.edu.pk/apply)",
      "### Program Portfolio Offered in Fall 2026",
      "1. **Faculty of Computer Science & Information Technology:**\n   - BS Computer Science (BSCS), BS Software Engineering (BSSE), BS Information Technology (BSIT), BS Data Science, and BS Cyber Security.\n   - 2-Year Associate Degrees in Computer Science, Database Management Systems, and Web Design & Development.\n\n2. **Faculty of Management & Business Studies:**\n   - Bachelor of Business Administration (BBA - 4 Years), BS Accounting & Finance, BS Banking & Finance, and BS Commerce.\n   - 2-Year Associate Degrees in Accounting, Islamic Banking, Human Resource Management, and Sales & Marketing.\n\n3. **Faculty of Arts & Social Sciences:**\n   - BS English (Applied Linguistics), BS Psychology, BS Mass Communication, BS Sociology, and BS Economics.\n\n4. **Faculty of Education:**\n   - B.Ed (Honours) 4-Year, B.Ed 1.5-Year (for Master's holders), and B.Ed 2.5-Year (for 14-year degree holders).\n\n5. **Postgraduate & Specialization Diplomas:**\n   - 1-Year Diplomas in Applied Psychology, Computer Science, Banking, Big Data Analytics, and Human Resource Management.",
      "### Eligibility Prerequisite Overview",
      "- **For 4-Year BS Programs:** Minimum 45% to 50% marks in Intermediate (FA, FSc, ICS, I.Com) or equivalent from a recognized board.\n- **For Computing Programs:** Mathematics at Intermediate level is mandatory for BSCS and BSSE as per NCEAC guidelines.\n- **For Associate Degree Programs:** Minimum 45% marks in Intermediate (12 years of education).\n- **For B.Ed (1.5 Years):** Minimum 16 years of education (MA/MSc/BS) with at least 45% aggregate or 2.00 CGPA.\n- **Zero Semester Option:** Candidates who do not meet the minimum percentage criteria for specific programs can qualify by passing the VU Zero Semester.",
      "### Step-by-Step Online Application Procedure",
      "1. **Portal Registration:** Navigate to `https://www.vu.edu.pk/apply` and click *New Registration* using your valid CNIC / B-Form and email address.\n2. **Select Study Track:** Choose your preferred study program and mode of education (Home-Based with digital access or Campus-Based at your nearest VU campus).\n3. **Enter Educational Profile:** Input your Matriculation and Intermediate grades, roll numbers, and passing boards.\n4. **Upload Scanned Documents:** Attach passport-sized photograph, CNIC/B-Form copy, and academic transcripts (DMC/Certificates).\n5. **Generate & Pay Processing Fee:** Print the computerized **Rs. 500 Admission Processing Fee** challan voucher. Deposit via 1Link, ATM, JazzCash, EasyPaisa, or any designated commercial bank branch.\n6. **Finalize Submission:** Confirm fee deposit on the portal before **10 October 2026** (or **05 October 2026** for MS/MPhil applicants).",
      "### Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)",
      "**Q1: What is the last date to apply for Virtual University Fall 2026 admissions?**\nGeneral undergraduate, Associate Degree, B.Ed, and Diploma admissions close on **10 October 2026**. However, MS/M.Phil programs and Need-Based Scholarships close **TODAY, 05 October 2026**.\n\n**Q2: When will classes start for Fall 2026?**\nAcademic classes for the Fall 2026 semester officially commence on **12 October 2026**.\n\n**Q3: What is the admission processing fee at VU?**\nThe admission processing fee is **Rs. 500/-**, payable through bank challan or mobile banking.\n\n**Q4: Can I study completely from home at Virtual University?**\nYes. VU offers a fully accredited Home-Based study mode where lectures, assignments, and study materials are accessed online through the Learning Management System (LMS).\n\n**Q5: What is the deadline for credit transfer or course exemptions?**\nThe last date to submit applications for course exemption and transfer of credits is **10 October 2026**.\n\n**Q6: What is the last date to add or drop courses?**\nStudents can add, drop, or replace courses through course selection until **21 October 2026**."
